From: Petr Wozniak
Subject: crypto: mtk-eip93: aead setkey must take the template from alg.aead.base

mtk_aead_setkey() looks the algorithm template up with
container_of(..., alg.skcipher.base). On 6.12 with DMA_NONCOHERENT
(MT7621) struct crypto_alg is 128-byte aligned and its offset differs
between skcipher_alg (256) and aead_alg (128), so the template pointer
is 128 bytes off, flags read as 0 and setkey returns -EINVAL. Every
ESP state with authenc(hmac(*),cbc(aes)) offloaded to EIP93 fails with
"RTNETLINK answers: Invalid argument" (xfrm state add).

Tested on MikroTik RBM33G (OpenWrt 25.12.6, kernel 6.12.112): ESP
aes256-sha256 and aes128-sha1 states are accepted and run through
authenc(hmac(sha256-eip93),cbc(aes-eip93)); TCP over ESP between two
namespaces, content verified.

--- a/drivers/crypto/mtk-eip93/eip93-aead.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/mtk-eip93/eip93-aead.c
@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@
 	struct crypto_tfm *tfm = crypto_aead_tfm(ctfm);
 	struct mtk_crypto_ctx *ctx = crypto_tfm_ctx(tfm);
 	struct mtk_alg_template *tmpl = container_of(tfm->__crt_alg,
-				struct mtk_alg_template, alg.skcipher.base);
+				struct mtk_alg_template, alg.aead.base);
 	u32 flags = tmpl->flags;
 	u32 nonce = 0;
 	struct crypto_authenc_keys keys;
